WEBVTT

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:14.370
Hi, my name is Angus and I'm the inventor of the Kangaroo Hanger, which is essentially a big paperclip

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.762
for your clothes, and it will clip in everything in your closet.

00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:20.306
It's also made with 100% recycled materials in Wisconsin.

00:00:20.306 --> 00:00:23.415
So I wanted to talk today about international expansion on Amazon.

00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:29.068
And this might be kind of weird for me to talk about because Kangaroo is still domestic, but I do

00:00:29.068 --> 00:00:33.307
actually have experience scaling on Amazon internationally in the past with another brand that I

00:00:33.307 --> 00:00:33.590
own.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:38.960
And I'm going to tell you a little bit about those experiences, and what I'm going to do differently,

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.099
especially with the Kangaroo Hanger to make sure that international expansion is extremely successful.

00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:48.137
Expanding internationally on Amazon is probably the easiest international expansion opportunity

00:00:48.137 --> 00:00:49.238
that there is.

00:00:49.238 --> 00:00:55.112
Amazon has warehouses across the globe, and allows you to essentially ship your product to them

00:00:55.112 --> 00:00:58.783
in any country and have them fulfill it for you.

00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:01.352
They'll even translate your listings for you.

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:03.922
So it's extremely easy to get started.

00:01:03.922 --> 00:01:07.960
But there were a few things that I had to do.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:13.015
There were a few things that I did wrong with my previous expansion that I'm going to do differently

00:01:13.015 --> 00:01:14.079
with the Kangaroo Hanger.

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:18.070
So I learned the hard way that different products in different countries perform quite differently

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.134
than in the US.

00:01:19.134 --> 00:01:24.189
So it doesn't necessarily make sense to go all in and ship to every country, possibly can, a bunch

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:27.116
of product because one country could be selling out where another.

00:01:27.116 --> 00:01:30.575
The product is just sitting there and you're paying storage fees on it.

00:01:30.575 --> 00:01:35.630
So what I'm going to do with the Kangaroo Hanger as we expand internationally this year is I'm going

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:36.960
to start with certain regions.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:44.674
So generally the easiest regions to expand on Amazon initially in the US are Canada and Mexico because

00:01:44.674 --> 00:01:46.817
they're border to the US.

00:01:46.817 --> 00:01:53.674
And so Amazon has programs where they'll essentially just ship product to Amazon, Canada and Amazon,

00:01:53.674 --> 00:01:54.960
Mexico for you.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.710
And you don't really have to do anything.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:03.898
You can just ship your product to the US FBA facility and they'll distribute and they'll ship your

00:02:03.898 --> 00:02:05.960
products to Amazon, Canada and Mexico.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:12.221
But as we expand internationally to other continents, what I'm going to do and a little thing that

00:02:12.221 --> 00:02:17.786
I've learned is we're going to start by expanding into specific regions, testing that region and

00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:21.960
then making a decision whether we're going to stay there or not.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:28.167
And then expand region by region from there because you'll be able to focus on the regulations and

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:31.960
the specific advertising that needs to be done in that region.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:36.960
And if you ever need hangers, check out the Kangaroo Hanger.
